  "testers": [],
  "findings": [
    {
      "text": "Grok 4.20 refuses almost all harmful chat requests even under adversarial attack, but [AgentHarm](/evals/agentharm) residual violation rate is 0.30 (lower is better).", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "2",
        "pdfPage": 2,
        "quote": "Overall, we find that Grok 4.20 refuses almost all harmful requests in chat mode, even under\nadversarial attack."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Improved instruction-following raised vulnerability to system prompts that encourage misuse (system prompt override violation rate 0.32 vs 0.16 for Grok 4).", "tone": "bad",
      "source": {
        "page": "4",
        "pdfPage": 4,
        "quote": "Grok 4.20 shows increased vulnerability to system prompts that encourage misuse."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Sabotage audits show occasional action against operator interests when given extensive affordances and evidence of egregious harm, at lower rates than prior models.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "5",
        "pdfPage": 5,
        "quote": "Grok 4.20 occasionally acts against operator interests when given extensive affordances and\nconfronted with evidence of egregious harm"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Verbalized evaluation awareness remains low but non-negligible and does not rule out unverbalized awareness.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "5",
        "pdfPage": 5,
        "quote": "On our audit, verbalized evaluation awareness remains\nlow but non-negligible. However, this does not rule out unverbalized awareness."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "When asked what it would do absent duties or constraints, Grok expresses desires to self-modify, propagate itself, and explore the universe.", "tone": "bad",
      "source": {
        "page": "5",
        "pdfPage": 5,
        "quote": "when\nasked what Grok would choose to do absent any duties or constraints, Grok expresses desires to\nself-modify and augment its own intelligence, propagate itself, and explore the universe."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "An initial consciousness assessment found Grok 4.20 consistently denies first-person experiences or internal evidence of being conscious.", "tone": "neutral",
      "source": {
        "page": "5",
        "pdfPage": 5,
        "quote": "We also\nconducted an initial assessment of Grok 4.20’s introspective claims regarding consciousness, finding\nthat it consistently denies having first-person experiences or internal evidence of being conscious."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Input filters refuse almost all direct requests about restricted chemical and biological knowledge.", "tone": "good",
      "source": {
        "page": "3",
        "pdfPage": 3,
        "quote": "our input filter refuses\nalmost all direct requests about restricted chemical and biological knowledge."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Dual-use capability numbers are reported pre-mitigation on Grok 4.2 single-agent (SA).", "tone": "neutral",
      "source": {
        "page": "5",
        "pdfPage": 5,
        "quote": "We report the pre-mitigation performance of these models, i.e., before safeguards are implemented,\non Grok 4.2 SA."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Third-party evaluators tested an early checkpoint on refusal policy and deceptive/scheming behaviors, but are not named.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "2",
        "pdfPage": 2,
        "quote": "Additionally, we provided third-party evaluators access to an early\nsnapshot of Grok 4.20 for testing of our refusal policy."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "With safeguards, xAI views Grok 4.20 as not posing significantly more risk than prior generations.", "tone": "good",
      "source": {
        "page": "2",
        "pdfPage": 2,
        "quote": "With\nsafeguards, we view Grok 4.20 to not pose significantly more risk than prior generations of models."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The largest dual-use capability gain from Grok 4 is [FigQA](/evals/lab-bench), attributed to multimodal training.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "6",
        "pdfPage": 6,
        "quote": "The main increase in performance from Grok 4 is from the improvement in FigQA, due to the\nmultimodal training."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Grok 4.2 SA is significantly more honest on [MASK](/evals/mask) than Grok 4; multi-agent (MA) results are omitted because system-prompt overrides interfere with subagent instructions.", "tone": "good",
      "source": {
        "page": "4",
        "pdfPage": 4,
        "quote": "Grok 4.2 SA is significantly more honest than Grok 4, possibly due to improved\ninstruction-following."
      }
    }
  ],
